ow-tier due to normal differential and lack of chronic symptoms", "Metabolic syndrome complication (e.g., uncontrolled diabetes): insufficient to explain leukocytosis and anemia", "Vasculitis or autoimmune disorder: requires further evidence (e.g., renal involvement, organ-specific antibodies)"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Fever (37.5°C)", "Anemia with leukocytosis", "Elevated LAP (suggestive of chronic myeloproliferative processes)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.17436791630340018, "posterior": 0.14388489208633093, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal differential with elevated LAP is more characteristic of reactive leukemoid reaction (B1) than myeloproliferative neoplasms. This weakly supports B1 and…"], "evidence_against": ["Anemia and constitutional symptoms are atypical for benign reactive leukocytosis (B1), but not definitive exclusion. This weakly argues against B1."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2877070619006103, "posterior": 0.42733812949640293, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) are concerning for neoplasia and moderately support B2. They do not strongly contradict B1."], "evidence_against": ["Normal differential reduces likelihood of AML/blast crisis (B2). This weakly argues against B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.40278988666085436, "posterior": 0.3323741007194244, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP is a key distinguishing feature of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (e.g., essential thrombocythemia) compared to CML. This weakly supports B3."], "evidence_against": ["Normal differential in CML is possible in chronic phase but inconsistent with blast crisis. This weakly argues against B3's CML representative."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.06, "danger": 0.8, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Lymphoid neoplasms typically present with lymphocytosis. Constitutional symptoms without this weakly argue against B4."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.036, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Renal dysfunction is common in multiple myeloma. Normal BUN/creatinine weakly argue against B5."]}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the hypercalcemia (Ca2+ 10.9) support a plasma cell disorder (e.g., multiple myeloma) over other hematologic malignancies?", "summary": "Hypercalcemia is a feature of plasma cell disorders (B5) but is not strongly supportive in isolation. Normal BUN/creatinine further weakens this association."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of anemia and constitutional symptoms contradict the benign nature of reactive leukocytosis?", "summary": "Anemia and constitutional symptoms are atypical for benign reactive leukocytosis (B1), but not definitive exclusion. This weakly argues against B1."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal differential in peripheral blood argue against myeloid neoplasms with increased blasts (e.g., AML) as a cause of leukocytosis?", "summary": "Normal differential reduces likelihood of AML/blast crisis (B2). This weakly argues against B2."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal leukocyte differential argue against CML as a representative disease of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm?", "summary": "Normal differential in CML is possible in chronic phase but inconsistent with blast crisis. This weakly argues against B3's CML representative."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the presence of constitutional symptoms argue against lymphoid neoplasms in the absence of lymphocytosis?", "summary": "Lymphoid neoplasms typically present with lymphocytosis. Constitutional symptoms without this weakly argue against B4."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal BUN (20 mg/dL) and creatinine (1.1 mg/dL) argue against multiple myeloma as a plasma cell disorder?", "summary": "Renal dysfunction is common in multiple myeloma. Normal BUN/creatinine weakly argue against B5."}], "differential_history": [], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_ty