ow-tier due to normal differential and lack of chronic symptoms", "Metabolic syndrome complication (e.g., uncontrolled diabetes): insufficient to explain leukocytosis and anemia", "Vasculitis or autoimmune disorder: requires further evidence (e.g., renal involvement, organ-specific antibodies)"], "alarm_features": ["Unintentional weight loss", "Fever (37.5°C)", "Anemia with leukocytosis", "Elevated LAP (suggestive of chronic myeloproliferative processes)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.14388489208633093, "posterior": 0.11602713352088101, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal differential with elevated LAP is more characteristic of reactive leukemoid reaction (B1) than myeloproliferative neoplasms. This weakly supports B1 and…"], "evidence_against": ["Anemia and constitutional symptoms are atypical for benign reactive leukocytosis (B1), but not definitive exclusion. This weakly argues against B1."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.42733812949640293, "posterior": 0.14369318351661858, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Subacute constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss) are concerning for neoplasia and moderately support B2. They do not strongly contradict B1."], "evidence_against": ["Normal differential reduces likelihood of AML/blast crisis (B2). This weakly argues against B2."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], 